  "summary": "Independently reviewed the research and controlled text for the GPT 1962 Seventeenth Sunday after Pentecost, 20 September 2026: checked the Missal's printed 398\u2013400, calendar LI, rubric 111(b) and Trinity Preface 293 against images; Pustet 1862 printed 341\u2013342 and Cummiskey 1861 printed 431\u2013433 against images; the seven complete retained Douay\u2013Rheims contexts; the principal retained Augustine, Chrysostom, Jerome, Thomas and Bellarmine loci; source bindings and same-family external dependencies; and the dated entries at https://www.fssp.fr/ordo-du-mois/ and https://icrspfrance.fr/ordo.php; RES-001 is withdrawn after independently reopening both Gospel images at original resolution, because Pustet printed 342 does include 'et' at the right end of the line 'tuum ex toto corde tuo, et', matching the 1962 wording and disproving my initial reading. PASS with no findings authorizes drafting the three distinct, compatible, whole-formulary interpretations with their individual four senses and substantive contributions from multiple checked authors, within the recorded universal-calendar scope, abridged historical translations, uncollated Jerome/Bellarmine transcriptions, excluded unverified leads and canonical-versus-liturgical English boundaries; this is bounded research acceptance, not exhaustive scholarship or acceptance of publication prose."
